WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:14.339
Good morning, ladies and gentlemen, and welcome
to this meeting in public of the Board of

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:15.639
NHS England.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:20.910
A very warm welcome to those members of the
public who have joined us here in the meeting

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:28.840
room in London, and also to our global audience
as we stream the proceedings live, just simply

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.500
as testament to our commitment to doing our
formal business in public.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.379
By the way, that means, particularly on this
morning’s agenda, there are some very chunky,

00:00:38.379 --> 00:00:45.160
difficult items that we will be discussing
and coming to a decision on.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.520
Just to emphasise again that the Board works
in many ways, and we try to ensure that non-executives

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.710
and executive members of the Board come together
in early-stage discussions about the future

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.480
strategy for NHS England.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.350
For example, we had a development session
yesterday afternoon where we looked at progress

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:09.829
on various fronts and tried to think our way
through some very important issues such as

00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:13.369
the future of the devolution agenda, for example.

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:20.469
Those are by and large items that will come
to future meetings of the Board of NHS England.

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:35.779
So this morning, welcome to the meeting of

00:01:35.779 --> 00:01:37.310
the Board.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:40.641
Also, to emphasise what the meeting is.

00:01:40.641 --> 00:01:41.649
It is a meeting in public.

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:47.729
It is not a public meeting; it is a meeting
in which the Board will be discussing.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:51.899
We will not be engaging in broader discussion,
but if anybody who is here in the audience

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:56.219
today would like to discuss with us after
the meeting any of these items informally,

00:01:56.219 --> 00:01:58.939
we would be very pleased to do so.

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:06.799
I am going to declare now the meeting formally
opened, and to invite from my colleagues any

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:09.850
declarations of interest in matters on the
agenda.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:16.780
I need to make a declaration, which is in
respect of the paper on congenital heart disease,

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.250
which makes reference to two organisations.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:25.560
One is the National Institute for Cardiovascular
Outcomes Research, and the other one is the

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:31.640
Clinical Operational Research Unit, both of
them based at UCL, of which I was the president

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:32.640
and provost.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.500
Just to assure the Board I have had no engagement
with either of those two organisations since

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.820
I retired from UCL two years ago.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:44.820
May I invite any other declarations of interest
from the Board?

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:52.290
It is a similar declaration, in the sense
that I set up NICOR when I was at UCL.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:56.160
The Congenital Heart Disease Review; I have
had a longstanding relationship with the team

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.540
in Newcastle and nationally, but I have not
had any direct involvement with this report.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.760
Good, thank you.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.400
Any other declarations of interest?

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.920
This is in addition, of course, to those standing
declarations which are recorded on the register.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.610
Good, thank you very much.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:14.180
I now would like to record apologies for absence.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.220
We have an apology from David Roberts.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.330
Just to emphasise, yet again, that this is
a conflict of timing.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:26.510
Today, David will be at the Annual General
Meeting of Nationwide, where he will be declared

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.430
to be the new chairman of Nationwide.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:35.210
So is not able to be with us this morning,
but he has had an input to the business of

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.320
the Board.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.730
We have at item 12 reports from Board Committees.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:47.140
Normally, these are starred items, and I invite
members of the Board to unstar them.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:51.730
I understand that what we would wish to do
this morning is to take three of them as simple

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:57.010
reports which are taken as read, but on the
Specialised Services Committee I will invite

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.950
Gordon to say a few words about the recent
deliberations of that Committee.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:04.550
Can I just stress to the Board to anybody
who wants to unstar any of those items through

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:11.560
the meeting when we get to there, that is
entirely within our power.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:17.670
May I then move on to the minutes of the last
meeting and ask you to approve them as an

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.419
accurate record?

00:04:19.419 --> 00:04:20.419
Thank you.

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:22.420
I have had no notice of any matters arising.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.540
Are there any other matters arising?

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.939
No, there are not.

00:04:25.939 --> 00:04:27.780
Thank you very much.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.370
Before we move to the Chief Executive’s
Report, may I just raise one or two preliminary

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.620
items from the Chair?

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:42.460
The first of them is to record the indication
that we have from Dame Barbara Hakin of her

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:49.280
retirement, and to ask the Board to support
my proposal that we at this stage record our

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.009
warmest thanks to Barbara for everything that
she has done.

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:56.539
I have to say that, personally, I have worked
with Barbara quite closely over the last four

00:04:56.539 --> 00:05:02.550
years, and I think much of my task would have
been much more difficult if not undoable without

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:07.599
the constant personal and warm support that
I have had from Barbara, who has worked in

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:11.919
the NHS in many various guises for over 40
years.

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:14.189
It is an extraordinary career.

00:05:14.189 --> 00:05:19.229
Barbara, we are not losing you yet, but it
would be I think wrong for us not this morning

00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:25.990
to record our enormous gratitude and appreciation
for all that you have done.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:32.699
Second, by way of preliminary business, is
to report, following the speech by the Secretary

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:40.409
of State last week, on the proposal that the
government has to draw together TDA and Monitor,

00:05:40.409 --> 00:05:48.240
and to have appointed as the Chairman of the
new organisation Ed Smith, who presently serves

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:54.499
on this Board as our Vice Chairman, and also
Chair of Audit and Risk Committee.

00:05:54.499 --> 00:05:58.460
I think it is obvious to everybody that there
could not have been a better choice of chairman,

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.849
whilst at the same time, we appreciate the
sheer complexity of the role, and frankly,

00:06:03.849 --> 00:06:12.199
the sheer importance of the new body NHS Improvement
in assisting us in partnership with them to

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:17.310
deliver more effectively the mission that
we all share, which is improving the quality

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:21.749
and efficiency of the NHS for patients across
the country.

00:06:21.749 --> 00:06:27.249
We will lose Ed I think probably about the
end of October, because I am very keen that

00:06:27.249 --> 00:06:33.639
we should have a transition, and I will be
discussing with members of the Board the implications

00:06:33.639 --> 00:06:37.559
and the knock-on consequences for activity
within the Board.

00:06:37.559 --> 00:06:43.270
Ed, at this stage, may we please extend to
you our warmest congratulations on that appointment

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:49.590
and our determination to continue to work
closely with you.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:54.839
Just very briefly to note that in the New
Year’s Honours List this year, there were

00:06:54.839 --> 00:07:01.189
awards of a knighthood to Ciarán Devane,
a citation which particularly mentions his

00:07:01.189 --> 00:07:06.919
outstanding contribution to supporting cancer
patients at Macmillan Cancer Support.

00:07:06.919 --> 00:07:15.000
In 2013, Macmillan reached 5.2 million people
and recruited 405,000 new supporters.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:22.499
That I think is a wonderful public recognition
of a superb career and those qualities that

00:07:22.499 --> 00:07:24.300
you have also brought to our Board, Ciarán.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.520
Our warmest congratulations to you.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:32.599
I would join in those congratulation Richard
Jeavons, who has been our Director for Specialised

00:07:32.599 --> 00:07:36.349
Commissioning on secondment, who was awarded
a CBE.

00:07:36.349 --> 00:07:43.719
If I am in such wonderful territory, I might
just touch upon the University of Birmingham,

00:07:43.719 --> 00:07:49.050
which is one of the finest talent-spotting
organisations in the country, because at its

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:55.520
honorary degree ceremony last week it conferred
honorary degrees upon Ed Smith, Simon Stevens

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:01.830
and Victor, and the Board I think would like
to reflect the hat-trick that is represented

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.389
in the University of Birmingham’s proceedings.

00:08:03.389 --> 00:08:09.999
And the discovery of the oldest copy of the
Quran was unrelated to that set of activities;

00:08:09.999 --> 00:08:10.999
important nonetheless.

00:08:10.999 --> 00:08:15.460
Well, I think we all recognise that the University
of Birmingham is one of the finest universities

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:16.419
in the country.

